// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// `at` reads its list unchecked below, since its parameter states it is at
// least 0, and that trust is a guard its callers pay as `Trap` or pass to
// the parameter their own proof stood on. `back` hands `at` a difference.
// A difference is a computed word, so the guard is charged at that call,
// and `main`, which hands `back` a number nothing bounds, cannot be
// `!Trap`. A compiler that read a difference as out of sight dropped the
// guard: it accepted this program, and the run stopped with a memory fault.
type ValidOffset = Int where 0 <= self

fn at(xs, i: ValidOffset) = if i < len(xs) { list_index(xs, i) } else { 0 }

fn back(pos: ValidOffset) = at([4, 5], pos - 0)

fn main(argv) with !Trap = back(len(argv) - 1000000)
